    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. so if i'm looking at a beam that's gonna span like 12 feet, what kind of safety factors or \"weak points\" should i be looking out for so i don't end up with structural failure? like where do things usually go wrong in these calculations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Key weak points often involve inadequate connection strength at beam-to-post joints or improper beam spanning ratios relative to the loading. Always confirm the span tables provided by your local engineering guide, as relying solely on basic estimations can be dangerous. Weather exposure, especially rot, can also significantly reduce the structural integrity of cedar over time, requiring post-treatment. For major spans, consulting a structural engineer is the safest way to ensure proper sizing and load management.",
      "source": "target",
